    {
      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "Let's denote the measures of the interior angles as 5x, 6x, and 7x, where x is a common multiplier.\n\nThe sum of the interior angles in any triangle is always 180 degrees. Therefore, we can set up the following equation:\n\n5x + 6x + 7x = 180\n\nCombining like terms, we get:\n\n18x = 180\n\nNow, divide both sides by 18 to solve for x:\n\nx = 180 / 18\nx = 10\n\nNow that we have the value of x, we can find the measure of the smallest interior angle:\n\nSmallest angle = 5x\nSmallest angle = 5 * 10\nSmallest angle = 50 degrees\n\nSo, the measure of the smallest interior angle is 50 degrees.",
